.TH ACCOUNT-INVENTORY 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "Unix Administration"
.SH NAME
account-inventory \- Inventory local or NSS-enumerated Unix users and groups
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaccount-inventory\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default scans /etc/passwd and /etc/group. NSS enumeration may omit remotely configured identities. Historical NIS compatibility records are skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --source local|nss
Select local files (default) or NSS enumeration. NSS is not guaranteed complete.
.TP
.B --kind users|groups|both
Select records.
.TP
.B --passwd-file PATH, --group-file PATH
Override local text files (not permitted with NSS mode).
.TP
.B --null
Emit seven NUL-separated fields per record.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Display program version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 completed, 1 malformed local data or traversal errors, 2 argument errors, 3 missing prerequisites.
.SH SEE ALSO
passwd(5), group(5), getent(1)
.SH AUTHOR
SASD Freeware contributors.
